  "wording_targets": [
    {
      "archived_excerpt": "The sections down to \"Frozen\" were committed before the runs.",
      "line": 4,
      "path": "research/NAE-LAYER-20261127-001/README.md",
      "report_fix": 6,
      "revision": "b2dc53d665e3649960bfcea756854a48ce6b968e"
    },
    {
      "archived_excerpt": "Under not-all-equal no law is a sum of others, so parity's facts (sums kept by every small change) have no analogue to lean on.",
      "line": 8,
      "path": "research/NAE-LAYER-20261127-001/README.md",
      "report_fix": 5,
      "revision": "b2dc53d665e3649960bfcea756854a48ce6b968e"
    },
    {
      "archived_excerpt": "Census start 959, the one start whose not-all-equal states admit a second presentation, is the record's Pasch pattern (its distinctions fall into three pairs no knot holds together; exchanging one pair's members exchanges the two presentations).",
      "line": 16,
      "path": "research/NAE-LAYER-20261127-001/README.md",
      "report_fix": 5,
      "revision": "b2dc53d665e3649960bfcea756854a48ce6b968e"
    },
    {
      "archived_excerpt": "**The census.** On all 7,075 starts the not-all-equal states form one class under single-distinction changes (C1) and no pair of distinctions is tied (C2); on all 6,845 starts with loose distinctions the loose patterns number 2^m \u2212 2 on the 15 tree-shaped ones and 2^m on the other 6,830 (C3); after one round all 2^m occur on all 500 starts read (C4). Under parity 2^(m \u2212 1) on every start (C3').",
      "line": 47,
      "path": "research/NAE-LAYER-20261127-001/README.md",
      "report_fix": 3,
      "revision": "b2dc53d665e3649960bfcea756854a48ce6b968e"
    },
    {
      "archived_excerpt": "**So, under not-all-equal.** A fact held by the whole is a relation among separately carried values that no proper part implies: on a part with no ring it exists (exactly two loose patterns missing), and it is the first knots' own law read through relays (whenever a relayed value is nonzero it fixes the first knot's distinction), not a new law. A ring erases it, and so does one round of growth, since growth's joins close rings. Nothing is kept by small changes (one class) and nothing is tied. **On the owner's rungs:** repetition, in the weak form of the first layer composed with itself; no second layer; and growth removes even the composed relation after one round. Under parity it is the reverse: rings carry the facts, and growth makes them last.",
      "line": 52,
      "path": "research/NAE-LAYER-20261127-001/README.md",
      "report_fix": 1,
      "revision": "b2dc53d665e3649960bfcea756854a48ce6b968e"
    },
    {
      "archived_excerpt": "Under not-all-equal nothing is kept by small changes and nothing is tied",
      "line": 8,
      "path": "research/NAE-LAYER-20261127-001/decision.md",
      "report_fix": 3,
      "revision": "b2dc53d665e3649960bfcea756854a48ce6b968e"
    },
    {
      "archived_excerpt": "The only relations are compositions over parts with no ring.",
      "line": 10,
      "path": "research/NAE-LAYER-20261127-001/decision.md",
      "report_fix": 1,
      "revision": "b2dc53d665e3649960bfcea756854a48ce6b968e"
    },
    {
      "archived_excerpt": "**Rings and growth erase them.** Closing a ring of five makes every loose pattern occur; after one round of growth every pattern occurs (the seven-knot tree, and all 500 census starts read).",
      "line": 13,
      "path": "research/NAE-LAYER-20261127-001/decision.md",
      "report_fix": 2,
      "revision": "b2dc53d665e3649960bfcea756854a48ce6b968e"
    },
    {
      "archived_excerpt": "**On the owner's rungs:** repetition in the weak form (the first layer composed with itself); no second layer; and growth removes even that. Under parity the reverse: rings carry the facts and growth makes them last.",
      "line": 15,
      "path": "research/NAE-LAYER-20261127-001/decision.md",
      "report_fix": 1,
      "revision": "b2dc53d665e3649960bfcea756854a48ce6b968e"
    },
    {
      "archived_excerpt": "Not-all-equal's whole-held relations are compositions that rings and growth erase",
      "line": 25,
      "path": "research/NAE-LAYER-20261127-001/decision.md",
      "report_fix": 2,
